IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `pa08-types`
IMPORT `pa08-status`
IMPORT `pa08-penalties`
IMPORT `pa08-goal`

-- Pensions Act 2008 (UK) — the encoder's tests. Expected values are worked
-- by hand from the Act.

§ `Tests`

GIVEN dob IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Worker facts`
`a worker born` dob MEANS `Worker facts` OF dob, Date 1 1 2057, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN pay IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Pay reference period`
`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` pay MEANS `Pay reference period` OF Date 1 4 2026, 12, pay

adult MEANS `a worker born` (Date 1 1 1990)

§§ `Goal 1 — status`

#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `to be automatically enrolled`
-- "more than £10,000": exactly £10,000 is not.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 10000) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 10001) EQUALS `to be automatically enrolled`
-- No qualifying earnings (not more than £6,240): s 9.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 6240) EQUALS `a worker who may ask to join under s 9`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 6241) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`
-- Aged 22 on 1 April 2026, or not until 2 April.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`a worker born` (Date 1 4 2004)) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `to be automatically enrolled`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`a worker born` (Date 2 4 2004)) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`
-- Aged 16 on 1 April 2026: a jobholder; 15: outside.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`a worker born` (Date 1 4 2010)) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`a worker born` (Date 2 4 2010)) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `not within the duties`
-- 75 on 1 April 2026: outside.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`a worker born` (Date 1 4 1951)) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `not within the duties`
-- Pensionable age reached: may opt in.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1959, Date 1 4 2026, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1959, Date 2 4 2026, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `to be automatically enrolled`
-- s 3(3)-(4); already in a qualifying scheme; not in Great Britain.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 1 2057, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `not within the duties`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 1 2057, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 1 2057, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 9000) EQUALS `not within the duties`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 1 2057, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS `not within the duties`
-- s 9(1)(c): already in a s 9 scheme.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` (`Worker facts` OF Date 1 1 1990, Date 1 1 2057, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) `in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 5000) EQUALS `not within the duties`
-- A monthly period: trigger £10,000/12; £900 is more.
#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`Pay reference period` OF Date 1 4 2026, 1, 900) EQUALS `to be automatically enrolled`
#ASSERT `the pension status of` adult `in` (`Pay reference period` OF Date 1 4 2026, 1, 800) EQUALS `a jobholder who may opt in`

§§ `Goal 2 — qualifying earnings and contributions`

#ASSERT `the qualifying earnings in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) EQUALS 23760
#ASSERT `the qualifying earnings in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 60000) EQUALS 44030
#ASSERT `the qualifying earnings in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 5000) EQUALS 0
-- One month: £1,000 − £520 = £480.
#ASSERT `the qualifying earnings in` (`Pay reference period` OF Date 1 4 2026, 1, 1000) EQUALS 480
-- Weekly-style: 6 months, £30,000 − £3,120 capped at £25,135: £22,015.
#ASSERT `the qualifying earnings in` (`Pay reference period` OF Date 1 4 2026, 6, 30000) EQUALS 22015
-- £23,760: employer 3% = £712.80, total 8% = £1,900.80.
#ASSERT `the contributions meet the quality requirement in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) `with` (`Contributions` OF 712.8, 1188, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the contributions meet the quality requirement in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) `with` (`Contributions` OF 700, 1300, TRUE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the contributions meet the quality requirement in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) `with` (`Contributions` OF 712.8, 1188, FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`the contributions meet the quality requirement in` (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000) `with` (`Contributions` OF 712.8, 1000, TRUE))

§§ `Goal 3 — penalty notices`

GIVEN start IS A DATE, rate IS A NUMBER, complied IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Penalty facts`
`penalties, escalating from` start `at` rate `until` complied MEANS
    `Penalty facts` OF Date 3 2 2026, 400, FALSE, FALSE, start, rate, complied

#ASSERT `the earliest payment date for` (`penalties, escalating from` (Date 3 3 2026) `at` 200 `until` (Date 13 3 2026)) EQUALS Date 3 3 2026
#ASSERT `the escalating penalty under` (`penalties, escalating from` (Date 3 3 2026) `at` 200 `until` (Date 13 3 2026)) EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the escalating penalty under` (`penalties, escalating from` (Date 2 3 2026) `at` 200 `until` (Date 13 3 2026)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the escalating penalty under` (`penalties, escalating from` (Date 3 3 2026) `at` 10001 `until` (Date 13 3 2026)) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the escalating penalty under` (`Penalty facts` OF Date 3 2 2026, 400, TRUE, FALSE, Date 3 3 2026, 200, Date 13 3 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the fixed penalty is within the limit in` (`Penalty facts` OF Date 3 2 2026, 50000, FALSE, FALSE, Date 3 3 2026, 200, Date 13 3 2026)
#ASSERT NOT (`the fixed penalty is within the limit in` (`Penalty facts` OF Date 3 2 2026, 50001, FALSE, FALSE, Date 3 3 2026, 200, Date 13 3 2026))

§§ `The top-level goal`

pos MEANS `the workplace pension position for` (`Workplace pension case` OF adult, (`a year from 1 April 2026 earning` 30000), JUST (`Contributions` OF 712.8, 1188, TRUE), NOTHING)
#ASSERT pos's `status` EQUALS `to be automatically enrolled`
#ASSERT pos's `qualifying earnings` EQUALS 23760
#ASSERT pos's `minimum employer contribution` EQUALS 712.8
#ASSERT pos's `minimum total contribution` EQUALS 1900.8
#ASSERT pos's `contributions meet the quality requirement` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT pos's `escalating penalty` EQUALS NOTHING
